      "text": "The as-cast AlCoCrFeNi2.1 alloy has a fine lamellar microstructure composed of coupled fcc and B2 phases.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4145285::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The fcc constituent of the starting alloy is specifically L12 ordered.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting lamellar microstructure is uniform.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting alloy's strength and plasticity are below industrial fastener requirements.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention is addition of 0.2 at.% Mo during melting and casting.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding 0.2 at.% Mo will refine and stabilize the lamellar fcc/B2 morphology.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding 0.2 at.% Mo may form Mo-rich nanoscale precipitates.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo-rich nanoscale precipitates would arrest dislocation motion and inhibit phase instability.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo addition will shift the phase balance by stabilizing the ductile fcc phase or precipitating a fine Mo-containing phase.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Refinement or restructuring of the lamellar duplex microstructure can improve the strength–ductility combination in AlCoCrFeNi2.1.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6353877::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo-induced phase or precipitation changes will increase yield strength and work hardening while maintaining or enhancing ductility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo addition will improve corrosion resistance and high-temperature stability.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed Mo-induced changes will mitigate degradation from thermal cycling, long-term loading, and room-temperature creep.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo-alloyed material will show yield- and tensile-strength improvements of approximately 3.6–34% relative to the baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo-alloyed material will show fracture elongation up to 0.9–2.9 times that of the baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo-alloyed material will have a lower room-temperature creep rate than the baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo-alloyed material will have improved corrosion resistance under fluctuating and high-temperature conditions.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed performance benefits will be maintained up to approximately 700°C.",
